    mechanics: "For token t with selected experts `idx[t, i]` and weights `w[t, i]`, `y_t = Σ_{i<k} w[t, i] · E_{idx[t,i]}(x_t)`. Weights are commonly normalized to sum to one (Mixtral: softmax over the selected logits; DeepSeek-V3: sigmoid affinities normalized over the selected set), so the output scale does not depend on k. With EP the combine is a reverse all-to-all carrying `[received_tokens, d_model]` outputs back to the source ranks; the weighted sum may be applied before sending (fewer bytes if it can fuse) or after receiving. The combine is commonly done in BF16 or FP32 accumulation even if experts ran in FP8, because summing k terms is sensitive to rounding. In backward, `∂L/∂w[t, i] = ⟨∂L/∂y_t, E_{idx}(x_t)⟩`, a dot product that trains the router, and `∂L/∂E_i(x_t) = w[t, i] · ∂L/∂y_t` flows to the experts. Tokens that were dropped by capacity limits contribute zero here and are carried only by the residual stream.",
