    summary: "Expert parallelism (EP) partitions the experts of each MoE layer across an EP group of devices, so a device with EP degree g stores `E / g` experts per layer. This is different from tensor parallelism, which slices every weight matrix across devices and needs an all-reduce per layer; EP keeps whole experts on single devices and needs an all-to-all to move tokens instead. EP is the main reason MoE models with hundreds of billions of total parameters are servable.",
